# THE ARITHMETIC SIBLING of D46's f-string whitelist arm — pre-existing, wider
# than equality, and closed as a side effect.
#
# The checker deliberately truncates most errors raised inside `f"{...}"` to a
# whitelist of kinds worth showing. `E_UnsupportedOperator` was not on it, so
# `print(f"{a + a}")` on a struct with no `Add` implementation COMPILED AND RAN
# at HEAD — silently, while the identical expression at `P c = a + a` was
# refused. Adding the kind for equality's sake closed the arithmetic half too.
#
# ⚠ THIS IS THE CELL THAT MAKES THE ARM'S SCOPE HONEST. The equality seed
# (`spectests/run/reject_eq_no_equatable_in_fstring.gg`) proves the whitelist
# retains `==`; only this one proves the arm is about the KIND and not about
# D46, so a later "narrow it back to equality" edit has something to trip.
#
# Asserted by `d46_fstring_arith_unsupported_rejects` in tests/integration.rs.

struct P:
    int a

void main():
    P a = P(1)
    print(f"{a + a}")
